  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN-Australia Counter Trafficking Program (ASEAN-ACT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN-Australia Counter-Trafficking program (ASEAN ACT) is a 10-year (2018&#x2013;28) investment which continues Australia&#x2019;s commitment to strengthening justice responses to trafficking in persons, the implementation of the ASEAN Convention against Trafficking in Persons, especially Women and Children among ASEAN Member States, and supporting partnership and cooperation at the regional and national levels. The program supports ASEAN&#x2019;s efforts to combat trafficking in persons through regional bodies including the ASEAN Senior Officials&#x2019; Meeting on Transnational Crime. ASEAN ACT also has established national-level programming in five ASEAN countries.</narrative>
  </description>
